  "strategy": "We approach the problem by optimizing a sequence over the probability simplex (sum normalized to 1) while focusing on minimizing the maximum auto-convolution coefficient. The sequence is chosen to be of length 512, as larger sequences (like 768) might be computationally expensive and 256-only sequences may lack sufficient complexity.\nOur method combines the Frank-Wolfe algorithm (constrained quadratic maximization) with adversarial attacks (coordinate-wise updates targeting the largest convolution peak) to beat the benchmark of 1.505008 to at least 1.49\u22481.5. We use dynamic endpoint and periodic resets with Gaussian and uniform perturbations to prevent accumulation of negative effects from coordinate-wise updates.",
